    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "II — Coordination",
      "estimated_duration_s": 22,
      "narration_text": "Agents talking to agents needs a topology, and that choice matters more than the protocol. Boss-worker isolates failure — you know whose message broke it — but the boss becomes the bottleneck. Pure peer-to-peer sounds elegant and produces endless loops of useless discussion. Whichever you pick, cap the message count, or two agents will talk forever.",
