    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "III — Cost",
      "estimated_duration_s": 22,
      "narration_text": "Not every task needs your best model. A classifier scores incoming complexity and routes it — simple work to something small and fast, hard reasoning to the expensive model. In high-volume systems that can halve the bill. The risk is the classifier itself: misjudge complexity and you either break hard tasks on weak models or burn reasoning tokens on trivia.",
