    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "IV — Reasoning",
      "estimated_duration_s": 21,
      "narration_text": "Instead of one chain of reasoning, generate several, score them, and prune the weak ones. It is how a chess player thinks — explore the variations, cut the bad lines, commit to the best. Genuinely powerful on hard diagnostic and mathematical problems. It also consumes tokens at a rate that makes it unusable for anything interactive.",
