    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "act": "VI — Safety",
      "estimated_duration_s": 22,
      "narration_text": "Guardrails are a perimeter, not a prompt. Redact personal information before it ever reaches a hosted model. Detect injections upstream. Moderate what comes back out. And for consumer apps the strongest move is structural — replace the open text box with canned journeys and most of the attack surface simply disappears. The cost is latency and false positives.",
